Build Specification — App 3: PROV-O Exporter and Importer
Completeness status: COMPLETE. All sections delivered in one pass. No truncation. Formatted for copy-paste into another conversation window. No tables, no boxes.

What It Is
A library that converts a STAG annotation record to and from PROV-O. It maps state nodes to prov:Entity, event nodes to prov:Activity, derived-from edges to prov:wasDerivedFrom, and revisions to prov:wasRevisionOf, and reverses the mapping on import. It takes in a STAG JSON record or a PROV-O document, and puts out the other of the two. It is for linked-data pipelines and provenance stores.

Core Requirements
Functional requirements:

Export a STAG JSON record to PROV-O.

Import a PROV-O document to a STAG JSON record.

Map state nodes to prov:Entity.

Map event nodes to prov:Activity.

Map derived-from edges to prov:wasDerivedFrom.

Map revision relations to prov:wasRevisionOf.

Map annotation records to prov:Entity with prov:wasGeneratedBy.

Map regime-qualified state records to distinct prov:Entity instances sharing one node ID.

Map self-loops with regime change to the correct PROV-O structure.

Preserve the full annotation record through a round trip (export then import returns the original record, modulo PROV-O expressiveness limits).

Support Turtle and JSON-LD serializations.

Operate as a library with a stable API.

Non-functional requirements:

Deterministic: same input produces same output.

No network dependency.

Fast: convert a typical annotation record in under one second.

Versioned: each schema version has a corresponding PROV-O mapping version.

Round-trip fidelity: report any information that cannot be preserved through PROV-O.

Input Specification
Input 1. STAG JSON record. Required for export. The annotation record conforming to Artifact 2, Appendix B.1.

Input 2. PROV-O document. Required for import. Turtle or JSON-LD.

Input 3. Serialization format. Optional for export. Values: turtle (default), jsonld, ntriples.

Input 4. Schema version. Required. Selects the correct PROV-O mapping version.

Input 5. Round-trip mode. Optional for export. Values: strict (fail if any field cannot be mapped), lossy (map what can be mapped and report the rest), extended (use STAG-specific PROV-O extensions for fields that have no standard mapping).

Output Specification
Output 1. PROV-O document. Turtle, JSON-LD, or N-Triples. For export.

Output 2. STAG JSON record. For import.

Output 3. Mapping report. JSON. Lists each STAG field and its PROV-O mapping, or "unmapped" if no mapping exists.

Output 4. Round-trip fidelity report. JSON. Lists any information lost in a round trip.

Output 5. Error report. JSON. Lists any mapping failures with the offending field and the reason.

Module-by-Module Specification
Module 1: STAG Record Loader
Reads the STAG JSON record. Validates it against the JSON Schema for the selected version. Rejects malformed records with an error report.

Module 2: PROV-O Document Loader
Reads the PROV-O document. Parses Turtle, JSON-LD, or N-Triples into an RDF graph. Validates that the graph contains the expected PROV-O structure. Rejects malformed documents.

Module 3: Mapping Table
Holds the mapping between STAG fields and PROV-O terms. Versioned per schema version. Provides lookup in both directions.

The mapping is:

State node maps to prov:Entity.

Event node maps to prov:Activity.

Derived-from edge maps to prov:wasDerivedFrom.

Revision relation maps to prov:wasRevisionOf.

Annotation record maps to prov:Entity with prov:wasGeneratedBy.

Regime-qualified state record maps to prov:Entity with prov:specializationOf pointing to the base node entity.

Self-loop with regime change maps to a prov:Activity with prov:used pointing to the source regime-qualified entity and prov:generated pointing to the target regime-qualified entity.

Node tuple (S, M, G) maps to STAG-specific properties on the prov:Entity: stag:system_scope, stag:model, stag:granularity.

Partition ID and version map to stag:partition_id and stag:partition_version.

Display label and anchoring status map to stag:derived_display_label and stag:evidential_anchoring.

Flags map to stag:not_determinable_flag, stag:provisional_flag, stag:threshold_sensitive_flag, stag:regime_not_determinable, stag:identity_partition_sensitive.

Module 4: Exporter
Takes a STAG JSON record. Applies the mapping table. Produces an RDF graph. Serializes to the requested format. Emits a mapping report.

The exporter handles the following cases:

Simple state node. Creates a prov:Entity with the STAG properties.

Regime-qualified state node. Creates two prov:Entity instances sharing one node ID, with prov:specializationOf pointing from the regime-qualified entity to the base entity.

Self-loop with regime change. Creates a prov:Activity with prov:used and prov:generated pointing to the two regime-qualified entities.

Event node. Creates a prov:Activity with prov:used pointing to the source entities and prov:generated pointing to the target entities.

Derived-from edge. Creates a prov:wasDerivedFrom triple.

Revision relation. Creates a prov:wasRevisionOf triple.

Supersession chain. Creates a chain of prov:wasRevisionOf triples.

Module 5: Importer
Takes an RDF graph. Applies the mapping table in reverse. Produces a STAG JSON record. Emits a mapping report.

The importer handles the following cases:

prov:Entity with STAG properties. Creates a state node.

prov:Activity with prov:used and prov:generated. Creates an event node or a self-loop.

prov:wasDerivedFrom triple. Creates a derived-from edge.

prov:wasRevisionOf triple. Creates a revision relation.

prov:specializationOf triple. Merges regime-qualified entities into a single node with regime attributes.

Module 6: Round-Trip Checker
Exports a STAG record, imports the result, and compares the two. Reports any differences. Classifies differences as expected (PROV-O expressiveness limits) or unexpected (bugs).

Module 7: Mapping Reporter
Produces the mapping report. Lists each STAG field, its PROV-O mapping, and whether the mapping is exact, approximate, or unmapped.

Module 8: Error Handler
Collects mapping failures. Produces the error report. In strict mode, fails on the first unmapped field. In lossy mode, continues and reports all unmapped fields.

