6.2 PROV-O to STAG
The reverse mapping applies the same table in reverse. The importer reads prov:Entity, prov:Activity, prov:wasDerivedFrom, prov:wasRevisionOf, and prov:specializationOf triples, and reconstructs the STAG record.

Special handling:

prov:specializationOf. When two prov:Entity instances share a node ID and one has prov:specializationOf pointing to the other, the importer merges them into a single node with regime attributes.

prov:Activity with prov:used and prov:generated. When a prov:Activity has one prov:used and one prov:generated and the two entities share a node ID, the importer creates a self-loop with regime_change.

prov:Activity with multiple prov:used. When a prov:Activity has two or more prov:used and one or more prov:generated, the importer creates an event node.

prov:wasRevisionOf chain. The importer reads the chain and populates supersedes and superseded_by.

Core Logic as Executable Pseudocode
7.1 Main Export Flow
function exportToPROVO(stagRecord, options):

Step 1. validate(stagRecord, options.schemaVersion). If invalid, return {error: "invalid STAG record"}.

Step 2. graph = new RDFGraph().

Step 3. for each node in stagRecord.nodes: addStateNodeToGraph(graph, node, options).

Step 4. for each event in stagRecord.events: addEventNodeToGraph(graph, event, options).

Step 5. for each edge in stagRecord.edges: addEdgeToGraph(graph, edge, options).

Step 6. for each revision in stagRecord.revisions: addRevisionToGraph(graph, revision, options).

Step 7. serialized = serialize(graph, options.format).

Step 8. mappingReport = buildMappingReport(stagRecord, options).

Step 9. return {output: serialized, mappingReport}.

7.2 Add State Node to Graph
function addStateNodeToGraph(graph, node, options):

baseEntity = new prov:Entity(node.node_id).

baseEntity.add(stag:system_scope, node.S).

baseEntity.add(stag:model, node.M).

baseEntity.add(stag:granularity, node.G).

baseEntity.add(stag:partition_id, node.partition_id).

baseEntity.add(stag:partition_version, node.partition_version).

if node.regime_attribute.value != null:

regimeEntity = new prov:Entity(node.node_id + "@" + node.regime_attribute.value).

regimeEntity.add(prov:specializationOf, baseEntity).

regimeEntity.add(stag:regime, node.regime_attribute.value).

regimeEntity.add(stag:order_parameter, node.regime_attribute.order_parameter).

regimeEntity.add(stag:control_parameter_point, node.regime_attribute.control_parameter_point).

regimeEntity.add(stag:phase_diagram_source, node.regime_attribute.phase_diagram_source).

if node.regime_attribute.regime_not_determinable:

regimeEntity.add(stag:regime_not_determinable, true).

graph.add(baseEntity).

graph.add(regimeEntity).

else:

graph.add(baseEntity).

7.3 Add Event Node to Graph
function addEventNodeToGraph(graph, event, options):

activity = new prov:Activity(event.event_node_id).

for each source in event.source_nodes:

activity.add(prov:used, source).

for each target in event.target_nodes:

activity.add(prov:generated, target).

activity.add(stag:composition_kind, event.composition_kind).

graph.add(activity).

7.4 Add Edge to Graph
function addEdgeToGraph(graph, edge, options):

if edge.kind == "derived_from":

triple = new Triple(edge.source, prov:wasDerivedFrom, edge.target).

triple.add(stag:derivation_kind, edge.derivation_kind).

triple.add(stag:derivation_specification, edge.derivation_specification).

graph.add(triple).

else:

activity = new prov:Activity(edge.edge_id).

activity.add(prov:used, edge.source).

activity.add(prov:generated, edge.target).

activity.add(stag:transition_attributes, edge.attributes).

if edge.is_self_loop:

activity.add(stag:regime_change, edge.regime_change).

graph.add(activity).

7.5 Add Revision to Graph
function addRevisionToGraph(graph, revision, options):

triple = new Triple(revision.new_annotation, prov:wasRevisionOf, revision.old_annotation).

graph.add(triple).

7.6 Main Import Flow
function importFromPROVO(provoDocument, options):

Step 1. graph = parse(provoDocument, options.format). If parse error, return {error: "malformed PROV-O document"}.

Step 2. stagRecord = new STAGRecord().

Step 3. entities = graph.findEntities().

Step 4. for each entity in entities: addEntityToRecord(stagRecord, entity, graph).

Step 5. activities = graph.findActivities().

Step 6. for each activity in activities: addActivityToRecord(stagRecord, activity, graph).

Step 7. derivedFromTriples = graph.findTriples(prov:wasDerivedFrom).

Step 8. for each triple in derivedFromTriples: addDerivedFromToRecord(stagRecord, triple).

Step 9. revisionTriples = graph.findTriples(prov:wasRevisionOf).

Step 10. for each triple in revisionTriples: addRevisionToRecord(stagRecord, triple).

Step 11. specializationTriples = graph.findTriples(prov:specializationOf).

Step 12. for each triple in specializationTriples: mergeRegimeQualifiedEntities(stagRecord, triple).

Step 13. mappingReport = buildMappingReport(stagRecord, options).

Step 14. return {output: stagRecord, mappingReport}.

7.7 Add Entity to Record
function addEntityToRecord(stagRecord, entity, graph):

if entity.hasProperty(stag:system_scope) and entity.hasProperty(stag:model) and entity.hasProperty(stag:granularity):

node = new Node().

node.node_id = entity.id.

node.S = entity.getProperty(stag:system_scope).

node.M = entity.getProperty(stag:model).

node.G = entity.getProperty(stag:granularity).

node.partition_id = entity.getProperty(stag:partition_id).

node.partition_version = entity.getProperty(stag:partition_version).

stagRecord.addNode(node).

7.8 Add Activity to Record
function addActivityToRecord(stagRecord, activity, graph):

used = activity.getProperty(prov:used).

generated = activity.getProperty(prov:generated).

if used.length == 1 and generated.length == 1 and used[0] shares node ID with generated[0]:

selfLoop = new SelfLoop().

selfLoop.source = used[0].

selfLoop.target = generated[0].

selfLoop.regime_change = activity.getProperty(stag:regime_change).

stagRecord.addSelfLoop(selfLoop).

else:

event = new Event().

event.event_node_id = activity.id.

event.source_nodes = used.

event.target_nodes = generated.

event.composition_kind = activity.getProperty(stag:composition_kind).

stagRecord.addEvent(event).

7.9 Merge Regime-Qualified Entities
function mergeRegimeQualifiedEntities(stagRecord, triple):

baseEntity = triple.target.

regimeEntity = triple.source.

baseNode = stagRecord.findNode(baseEntity.id).

regimeNode = stagRecord.findNode(regimeEntity.id).

if baseNode != null and regimeNode != null:

baseNode.regime_attribute = regimeNode.regime_attribute.

stagRecord.removeNode(regimeEntity.id).

7.10 Round-Trip Check
function roundTripCheck(stagRecord, options):

Step 1. exportResult = exportToPROVO(stagRecord, options).

Step 2. importResult = importFromPROVO(exportResult.output, options).

Step 3. differences = compareRecords(stagRecord, importResult.output).

Step 4. classified = differences.map(d => classifyDifference(d)).

Step 5. return {differences: classified, expected: classified.filter(d => d.expected), unexpected: classified.filter(d => not d.expected)}.

Data Model / JSON Schema for Internal State
The library's internal state is an RDF graph and a STAG record. The mapping report is a JSON object:

mappingReport:

stagRecordId (string)

schemaVersion (string)

mappingVersion (string)

entries (array of mapping entry objects)

Each mapping entry:

stagField (string)

provoTerm (string or null)

mappingType (exact, approximate, unmapped)

note (string or null)

The round-trip fidelity report is a JSON object:

roundTripReport:

stagRecordId (string)

differences (array of difference objects)

expectedCount (integer)

unexpectedCount (integer)

Each difference:

fieldPath (string)

originalValue (any)

roundTrippedValue (any)

classification (expected, unexpected)

reason (string)

Architecture
Module breakdown:

STAG Record Loader. Reads and validates the STAG JSON record.

PROV-O Document Loader. Reads and parses the PROV-O document.

Mapping Table. Holds the bidirectional mapping.

Exporter. Converts STAG to PROV-O.

Importer. Converts PROV-O to STAG.

Round-Trip Checker. Exports, imports, and compares.

Mapping Reporter. Produces the mapping report.

Error Handler. Collects and reports errors.

Data flow:

For export: STAG record goes to STAG Record Loader. Mapping Table is consulted. Exporter produces the RDF graph. Serializer produces the output. Mapping Reporter produces the report.

For import: PROV-O document goes to PROV-O Document Loader. Mapping Table is consulted. Importer produces the STAG record. Mapping Reporter produces the report.

For round trip: Exporter produces PROV-O. Importer produces STAG. Round-Trip Checker compares.

